  "factor_name": "60-day residual trend quality reversal",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "-((return_60(asset) - cross_sectional_median(return_60)) / realized_vol_30).lag(1)",
    "description": "For each tradable asset, subtract the cross-sectional median 60-session return, divide by 30-session realized volatility, reverse the sign, lag one completed session, and standardize cross-sectionally. Higher values favor assets with relatively weak volatility-adjusted medium-term trends, consistent with the validated contrarian direction."
